CloudBurrow patch 91 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1764).

The emulator served the project it was started with (--project) alone and
answered every other one 404 "project P is not found", even a project the
instance's Resource Manager has. A request that carries the header
X-Cloudburrow-Known-Project now adds the project it names on first use,
empty, and the emulator serves it from then on as it serves the first:
datasets, tables, jobs, and queries that name another project's tables
(the engine keeps every project in one database, so `other.ds.t` already
resolved once both existed). Without the header nothing changes. The
front sets it once it has found the project ACTIVE in Resource Manager,
and removes it from its clients' requests.

cloudburrow_known_projects_test.go (TestKnownProjectAddedOnFirstUse):
another project is 404 without the header; with it, it is added, and its
datasets, tables, rows and jobs are served from then on, without the
header too; a job of the first project reads its table; two first uses
at once both succeed. It fails without the patch.

